    "answer": {
      "short": "Both. Changing the base preserves the value of the logarithm.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\log_2(7)&=\\frac{\\log_{10}(7)}{\\log_{10}(2)}\\\\\\log_2(7)&=\\frac{\\ln(7)}{\\ln(2)}.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth expressions represent the same value, so Bob and Mary will both get the correct answer.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
